 factor is e^{-x}, since the coefficient of S(x) is -1. Multiplying both sides by e^{-x}:\n\ne^{-x} S\u2019(x) - e^{-x} S(x) = e^{-x} f\u2080(x)\n\nThe left side is the derivative of (e^{-x} S(x)). So integrating both sides from 0 to x:\n\n\u222b\u2080\u02e3 d/dt [e^{-t} S(t)] dt = \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{-t} f\u2080(t) dt\n\nLeft side is e^{-x} S(x) - e^{0} S(0) = e^{-x} S(x) - S(0). But S(0) is the sum of f_n(0) for n \u2265 1. Let's check what f_n(0) is. For any n \u2265 1, f_n(0) = \u222b\u2080\u2070 f_{n-1}(t) dt = 0. Therefore, S(0) = 0. So left side is e^{-x} S(x). Therefore:\n\ne^{-x} S(x) = \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{-t} f\u2080(t) dt\n\nMultiply both sides by e^x:\n\nS(x) = e^x \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{-t} f\u2080(t) dt\n\nWhich matches the result we obtained earlier by interchanging the sum and integral. So that's the explicit formula. Therefore, the sum is e^x times the integral from 0 to x of e^{-t} f\u2080(t) dt.\n\nLet me verify this with an example. Suppose f\u2080(x) = 1, constant function. Then f\u2081(x) = x, f\u2082(x) = x\u00b2/2, f\u2083(x)=x\u00b3/6, etc. So the series is x + x\u00b2/2 + x\u00b3/6 + ... which is e^x - 1 (since the sum from n=1 to \u221e x^n/n! = e^x -1). According to the formula, S(x) = e^x \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{-t} *1 dt = e^x [ -e^{-t} ]\u2080\u02e3 = e^x ( -e^{-x} +1 ) = e^x (1 - e^{-x}) = e^x -1, which matches. So that works.\n\nAnother example, if f\u2080(x) = e^{kx}, let's see. Then S(x) = e^x \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{-t} e^{kt} dt = e^x \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{(k-1)t} dt. If k \u22601, this is e^x [ e^{(k-1)x} / (k-1) - 1/(k-1) ) ] = e^x / (k-1) (e^{(k-1)x} -1 ) = [ e^{k x} - e^x ] / (k -1). On the other hand, computing the series: f\u2081(x)= \u222b\u2080\u02e3 e^{kt} dt = (e^{kx} -1)/k. f\u2082(x)= \u222b\u2080\u02e3 (e^{kt} -1)/k dt = (e^{kx} -1)/k\u00b2 - x/k. Hmm, not sure if it's easy to sum, but according to our formula, the sum should be [e^{kx} - e^x]/(k-1). Let me check for k=2. Then S(x) = [e^{2x} - e^x]/(2 -1) = e^{2x} - e