e \\(b_{k+i}\\) is understood modulo \\(n\\).\n\n4. **Sum these inequalities:**\n   Sum up all \\(n\\) inequalities corresponding to different \\(i\\) values:\n   \\[\n   \\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} (a_1 b_{1+i} + a_2 b_{2+i} + \\ldots + a_n b_{n+i}) \\leq n \\left(a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\ldots + a_n b_n \\right)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Combine terms:**\n   Notice that each term \\(a_k\\) appears exactly \\(n\\) times on the left-hand side:\n   \\[\n   a_1(b_1 + b_2 + \\ldots + b_n) + a_2(b_1 + b_2 + \\ldots + b_n) + \\ldots + a_n(b_1 + b_2 + \\ldots + b_n) \\leq n (a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\ldots + a_n b_n)\n   \\]\n   \n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   \\left(a_1 + a_2 + \\ldots + a_n\\right) \\left(b_1 + b_2 + \\ldots + b_n\\right) \\leq n \\left(a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\ldots + a_n b_n \\right)\n   \\]\n\n6. **Derive the final inequality:**\n   Divide both sides by \\(n\\) to get the required inequality:\n   \\[\n   a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\cdots + a_n b_n \\geq \\frac{1}{n} \\left( a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n \\right) \\left( b_1 + b_2 + \\cdots + b_n \\right)\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + \\cdots + a_n b_n \\geqslant \\frac{1}{n} \\left( a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots + a_n \\right) \\left( b_1 + b_2 + \\cdots + b_n \\right)}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Given an acute non-isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\), point \\(O\\) is the center of its circumscribed circle. The extension of the altitude \\(BH\\) of triangle \\(ABC\\) intersects its circumscribed circle at point \\(N\\). Points \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are marked on sides \\(AB\\) and \\(BC\\) respectively such that \\(OX \\parallel AN\\) and \\(OY \\parallel CN\\). The circumscribed circle of triangle \\(XBY\\) intersects segment \\(BH\\) at point \\(Z\\). Prove that \\(XY \\parallel OZ\\).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to prove that XY is parallel to OZ in this given geometric configuration. Let me start by understanding all the compone